{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>When brothers dwell.</b> This excludes brothers from the mother's side, for we derive a gezeirah shavah from 'brothers' — 'Twelve are your servants, brothers are we.'" "<b>And one of them dies.</b> The alef with patach." "<b>Her brother-in-law shall come upon her.</b> It is a mitzvah. Since she was included in the permitted and was forbidden and returned to permission, one might say she returns to her original permission; therefore it says 'her brother-in-law shall come upon her' — a mitzvah. Similarly: 'You shall eat it' etc., as I explained in the portion of Tzav." "<b>And her brother-in-law.</b> Of the letters it has two sides in their interpretation: one from this side reversed, the other like 'to fertilize it' (לדשנו). And similarly in the interpretation: 'he shall remove and take away' the levirate bond and she becomes his wife."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:13.797744437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}